# An ALLOWLIST, not a denylist. Everything is excluded and four paths are let
# back in.
#
# The reason is specific rather than tidiness: skulkd/_build and skulkd/deps on a
# developer's machine contain compiled BEAM files and, in argon2_elixir's case, a
# NIF compiled as a Mach-O shared object for macOS. Copied into a Linux image
# they would either be rebuilt (slow, silent) or loaded (fatal, at the first
# password hash rather than at build). A denylist protects against the paths
# somebody remembered; this protects against the ones they did not.
*

!skulkd/mix.exs
!skulkd/mix.lock
!skulkd/config
!skulkd/lib
